{
 "lines": [
  {
   "i": 0,
   "start": 3.5,
   "end": 8.385,
   "text": "The first night I babysat for the Hales, they left me one strange rule."
  },
  {
   "i": 1,
   "start": 8.985,
   "end": 14.127,
   "text": "If the baby monitor ever shows two cribs... don't go upstairs. Just call us."
  },
  {
   "i": 2,
   "start": 14.927,
   "end": 19.449,
   "text": "I laughed. One baby. One crib. One little camera on the shelf."
  },
  {
   "i": 3,
   "start": 20.149,
   "end": 24.693,
   "text": "By nine, she was asleep. The house was quiet, except for the rain."
  },
  {
   "i": 4,
   "start": 25.493,
   "end": 28.331,
   "text": "Around eleven, the screen flickered."
  },
  {
   "i": 5,
   "start": 29.931,
   "end": 31.104,
   "text": "Two cribs."
  },
  {
   "i": 6,
   "start": 32.504,
   "end": 38.008,
   "text": "In the second one, something was sitting up. Too long to be a baby. Too still to be a toy."
  },
  {
   "i": 7,
   "start": 38.808,
   "end": 42.605,
   "text": "I called the Hales. It rang... and rang... and rang."
  },
  {
   "i": 8,
   "start": 45.205,
   "end": 50.667,
   "text": "I didn't go upstairs. I just sat on the couch, staring at that grainy gray picture."
  },
  {
   "i": 9,
   "start": 51.367,
   "end": 54.204,
   "text": "Then I noticed what was wrong with it."
  },
  {
   "i": 10,
   "start": 55.404,
   "end": 58.604,
   "text": "The second crib wasn't in the nursery."
  },
  {
   "i": 11,
   "start": 59.604,
   "end": 63.124,
   "text": "It was in the living room... right behind my couch."
  },
  {
   "i": 12,
   "start": 64.924,
   "end": 66.887,
   "text": "And it was empty now."
  }
 ],
